5; κατὰ καιρόν, Rom.5:6; πρὸ καιροῦ, Mat.8:29 \n SYN.: (χρόνος) time in the sense of duration (AS)","source_line":2723}],"occurrence_count":85,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"tempo","count":64},{"gloss":"tempos","count":12},{"gloss":"oportunidade","count":3},{"gloss":"estações","count":2},{"gloss":"presente","count":1},{"gloss":"um-tempo","count":1},{"gloss":"tempo-presente","count":1},{"gloss":"avançada","count":1}]},"G2557":{"id":"G2557","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2557","disambiguated_id":"G2557 =","unique_id":"G2557","headword":"κακοῦργος","transliteration":"kakourgos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"criminal","definition_en":"κακοῦργος, -ον\n (contr. from epic κακόεργος), [in LXX. Pro.21:15 (אָוֶן, פָּעַל), Est.8:13, Sir.11:33 33:26 (Sir.33:26)* ;] \na malefactor, criminal: Luk.23:32-33, 39, 2Ti.2:9.†\n (AS)","source_line":2745}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"malfeitores","count":3},{"gloss":"criminoso","count":1}]},"G2755":{"id":"G2755","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2755","disambiguated_id":"G2755 =","unique_id":"G2755","headword":"κενόδοξος","transliteration":"kenodoxos","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"conceited","definition_en":"κενόδοξος, -ον\n (κενός, δόξα), \nvain-glorious: Gal.5:26.†\n (AS)","source_line":2945}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"vangloriosos","count":1}]},"G3644":{"id":"G3644","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3644","disambiguated_id":"G3644 =","unique_id":"G3644","headword":"ὀλοθρευτής","transliteration":"olothreutēs","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M","gloss_en":"destroyer","definition_en":"ὀλοθρευτής (Rec. όλ-), -οῦ, ὁ \n (ὀλοθρεύω), \na destroyer: 1Co.10:10 (not elsewhere).†\n (AS)","source_line":3760}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"destruidor","count":1}]},"G3930":{"id":"G3930","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3930","disambiguated_id":"G3930 =","unique_id":"G3930","headword":"παρέχω","transliteration":"parechō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to furnish occasion","definition_en":"παρ-έχω \n [in LXX: Psa.30:7 (עָמַד hi.), etc. ;] \n__I. Active voice., \n __1. to furnish, provide, supply; with ref. to incorporeal things, to afford, show, give, cause: with accusative, Act.22:2, 1Ti.1:4; with accusative and dative, Mat.26:10, Mrk.14:6, Luk.11:7 18:5, Act.16:16 17:31 28:2, Gal.6:17, 1Ti.6:17. \n __2. to present, offer: with accusative and dative, Luk.6:29; with prop. reflex. and accusative pred., to show or present oneself (see infr., and cf. B1., § 55, 1). \n __II. Middle voice., \n __1. to supply, furnish or display of one's own part: with accusative and dative, Luk.7:4, Act.19:24, Col.4:1. \n __2. In late writers, with prop. reflex. and accusative pred. (= act. ut supr.), to show or present oneself (Xen., FlJ, al.; cf. M, Pr., 248; Deiss., BS, 254) : Tit.2:7.†\n (AS)","source_line":4048}],"occurrence_count":16,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"causais","count":2},{"gloss":"oferece","count":1},{"gloss":"concederes","count":1},{"gloss":"dês","count":1},{"gloss":"causar","count":1},{"gloss":"dava","count":1},{"gloss":"tendo-dado","count":1},{"gloss":"lucro","count":1},{"gloss":"guardaram","count":1},{"gloss":"demonstraram","count":1},{"gloss":"perturbe","count":1},{"gloss":"concedei","count":1},{"gloss":"discussões","count":1},{"gloss":"que-concede","count":1},{"gloss":"apresentando","count":1}]},"G4146":{"id":"G4146","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4146","disambiguated_id":"G4146 =","unique_id":"G4146","headword":"πλουσίως","transliteration":"plousiōs","lexical_morphology":"G:ADV","gloss_en":"richly","definition_en":"πλουσίως \n adv., \nrichly, abundantly: Col.3:16, 1Ti.6:17. Tit.3:6, 2Pe.1:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":4271}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"abundantemente","count":4}]},"G4337":{"id":"G4337","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4337","disambiguated_id":"G4337 =","unique_id":"G4337","headword":"προσέχω","transliteration":"prosechō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to watch out","definition_en":"προσ-έχω \n [in LXX for קָשַׁב hi., שָׁמַר ni., etc. ;] \n__1. to turn to, bring to (frequently ναῦν, expressed or understood, to bring to port, land; Hdt., al.). \n __2. τ. νοῦν, before dative, to turn one's mind to, attend to; in Xen. and later writers with νοῦν omitted (El., § 53, 1; 81, 1): Act.8:6 16:14, Heb.2:1, 2Pe.1:19; in sense of caring or providing for, Act.20:28; π. ἑαυτῷ, to give heed to oneself (M, Pr., 157; cf. Gen.24:6, Exo.10:28, al.): Luk.17:3 21:34, Act.5:35; id. before ἀπό (M, Pr., 102; B1., § 34, 11; 40, 3; see: βλέπω), Luk.12:1; (without dative) Mat.7:15 10:17 16:6, 11-12, Luk.20:46 (cf. Sir.6:13, al.); before μή, with inf. (M, Pr., 193; Bl., § 69, 4), Mat.6:1. \n __3. to attach or devote oneself to: with dative of person(s), Act.8:10-11, 1Ti.4:1; with dative of thing(s), 1Ti.1:4 3:8 4:13 6:3 T (-ερχ-, WH, R), Tit.1:14, Heb.7:13.†\n (AS)","source_line":4467}],"occurrence_count":24,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"atenção","count":7},{"gloss":"tende","count":2},{"gloss":"tomai","count":2},{"gloss":"olhai","count":2},{"gloss":"guardai-vos","count":1},{"gloss":"tende-cuidado","count":1},{"gloss":"tomassem-cuidado","count":1},{"gloss":"guardai","count":1},{"gloss":"cuidai-de","count":1},{"gloss":"prestavam-atenção","count":1},{"gloss":"prestai-atenção","count":1},{"gloss":"cobiçosos","count":1},{"gloss":"persiste","count":1},{"gloss":"serviu","count":1},{"gloss":"prestardes-atenção","count":1}]},"G4438":{"id":"G4438","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4438","disambiguated_id":"G4438 =","unique_id":"G4438","headword":"πυκτεύω","transliteration":"pukteuō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to box","definition_en":"πυκτεύω\n (πύκτης, a pugilist), \nto box: 1Co.9:26.†\n (AS)","source_line":4571}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"luto","count":1}]},"G57":{"id":"G57","source":